  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one data point (rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 at ~48.5% accuracy), which is very low and gives us almost no information about which modality carries useful signal. The most critical uncertainty to resolve early is whether the image modality provides stronger or complementary signal compared to RNA. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_001: it swaps the modality while keeping profile setting (singleprofile) and encoder complexity (standard pretrained encoder) comparable. If image-only substantially outperforms RNA-only, we should prioritize image-centric or multimodal configurations in the remaining 8 experiments; if it is similarly poor, we know the bottleneck is representation quality rather than modality choice and should focus on stronger encoders (scgpt, ViT-L) or multiprofile aggregation. Resolving this modality question now prevents wasting budget on a suboptimal modality branch."
}

